WEBVTT

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:12.630
It's amazing every time I hear it.

00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:15.800
That's the London Symphony Orchestra for you.

00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:17.140
Yes.

00:01:17.140 --> 00:01:21.810
Their harmony with the violinist, Thomas Simpson, was splendid.

00:01:21.810 --> 00:01:26.310
Simpson is truly a genius born of London.

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:40.620
Mr. Simpson, it's time for an encore.

00:01:41.990 --> 00:01:45.000
I don't even have time for a cup of tea?

00:02:05.930 --> 00:02:08.390
It's Bach's Aria in G.

00:02:08.390 --> 00:02:10.480
Even I know this song.

00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:13.860
You can't do a song like this unless you're pretty sure of yourself.

00:03:09.540 --> 00:03:10.620
Mr. Simpson... Mr. Simpson!

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:12.080
Mr. Simpson... Mr. Simpson!

00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:15.090
Are you okay, Mr. Simpson?

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:46.240
I held my breath and kept waiting while my heart was scratched away

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:57.590
A minute, a second never felt so long

00:03:58.090 --> 00:04:09.350
I look up at the sky and ask the wind, "Can I fly now?"

00:04:09.560 --> 00:04:15.650
The weak person I was is no more

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:21.240
I decided to just believe

00:04:22.570 --> 00:04:28.370
With the dreams I once had in my hand now

00:04:28.370 --> 00:04:32.210
I go towards you

00:04:34.120 --> 00:04:39.920
Carrying those emotions I felt when I broke

00:04:39.920 --> 00:04:44.050
I go towards you

00:04:44.050 --> 00:04:48.100
Blown by the wind

00:04:48.850 --> 00:04:53.560
Oh blown

00:04:56.270 --> 00:05:00.440
A Shot in G

00:05:18.290 --> 00:05:22.300
Despite the issue being the unexpected accident of his G-string breaking,

00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:28.300
this has put an indelible stain on his 30-something-year history as a violinist.

00:05:30.140 --> 00:05:30.560
Damn.

00:05:36.560 --> 00:05:39.520
Mr. Simpson, the students are here.

00:05:39.400 --> 00:05:40.610
sub this? if not use normal leadout on last line

00:05:51.080 --> 00:05:52.660
Okay, stop.

00:05:52.660 --> 00:05:55.200
You should play it like this.

00:06:13.260 --> 00:06:15.470
I'm not feeling well today.

00:06:16.230 --> 00:06:17.520
Let's do this tomorrow.

00:06:19.900 --> 00:06:21.230
Why?

00:06:21.230 --> 00:06:23.690
Why can't I play in front of other people?

00:06:28.240 --> 00:06:34.240
You have no physical defects; it's either mild hysteria or the start of a psychosomatic illness.

00:06:34.910 --> 00:06:39.250
The best thing to do is to relax and forget it.

00:06:39.250 --> 00:06:41.290
You've gotta be kidding me!

00:06:41.290 --> 00:06:44.250
I can't remain calm in a time like this!

00:06:44.250 --> 00:06:48.760
See, that personality of yours is just adding pressure.

00:06:49.300 --> 00:06:51.760
Well, stay off your feet for a few days.

00:06:56.680 --> 00:07:00.140
You don't want me to appear in the charity concert?

00:07:00.730 --> 00:07:02.980
I hope you won't get upset.

00:07:02.980 --> 00:07:06.150
I'm worried about your health.

00:07:06.730 --> 00:07:10.780
There's nothing wrong with me physically, even the doctors say so.

00:07:10.780 --> 00:07:14.240
Anybody would panic during an accident like that.

00:07:14.240 --> 00:07:16.160
It was just one mistake.

00:07:16.620 --> 00:07:22.710
However, it's been two weeks, and you still can't play a perfect performance.

00:07:22.710 --> 00:07:26.170
You should rest and receive treatment.

00:07:26.170 --> 00:07:28.840
Why don't you say it straight?

00:07:28.840 --> 00:07:33.180
You can't perform with someone whose hand shakes when he holds a bow!

00:07:33.800 --> 00:07:36.640
That you'd rather have a junkie than that!

00:07:37.140 --> 00:07:38.180
Simpson...

00:07:39.600 --> 00:07:40.270
I-I'm sorry for yelling.

00:07:40.270 --> 00:07:43.190
I-I'm sorry for yelling.

00:07:43.690 --> 00:07:47.360
But who's going to play in my place?

00:07:48.150 --> 00:07:49.610
Guten?

00:07:49.610 --> 00:07:51.240
Archer?

00:07:51.240 --> 00:07:52.200
No...

00:07:52.200 --> 00:07:53.450
Who?

00:07:53.450 --> 00:07:54.530
Tell me.

00:07:56.830 --> 00:07:58.200
Kerensky.

00:07:59.330 --> 00:08:01.210
Kerensky?

00:08:01.210 --> 00:08:07.210
Yes, I think you know him. He's coming to our country on a concert tour.

00:08:07.880 --> 00:08:10.170
Why Kerensky?

00:08:10.170 --> 00:08:15.220
This concert has a history! Why are you inviting a Russian rival?

00:08:15.890 --> 00:08:19.220
Anybody but Kerensky, please!

00:08:22.100 --> 00:08:25.230
It's already been decided, Simpson.

00:08:48.250 --> 00:08:55.890
But Mr. Simpson, don't you think it's dangerous to carry this much cash?

00:08:55.890 --> 00:08:57.970
No, don't worry about it.

00:09:01.930 --> 00:09:06.770
I'll be going to the charity concert too.

00:09:12.740 --> 00:09:15.360
Chief, didn't you know?

00:09:16.990 --> 00:09:21.330
He was forced out of the charity concert.

00:09:21.330 --> 00:09:22.540
What did you say?

00:09:22.540 --> 00:09:28.500
That Russian, Kerensky, is going to be doing the solo in his place.

00:09:28.500 --> 00:09:30.460
I see...

00:09:44.180 --> 00:09:45.020
Yes.

00:09:45.020 --> 00:09:46.640
Is this Simpson?

00:09:46.640 --> 00:09:47.190
Y-Yes.

00:09:47.190 --> 00:09:48.190
Y-Yes.

00:09:48.190 --> 00:09:50.400
I'll be waiting at the London Eye.

00:09:50.400 --> 00:09:51.860
I understand.

00:10:03.910 --> 00:10:07.750
I hear you're the best in your field.

00:10:07.750 --> 00:10:09.920
Have you ever failed, even once?

00:10:13.500 --> 00:10:14.380
I see...

00:10:14.380 --> 00:10:16.380
I shouldn't have asked.

00:10:16.380 --> 00:10:20.930
I heard something from my friend in the SIS, the one who introduced me to you.

00:10:20.930 --> 00:10:23.430
You're a professional among professionals.

00:10:24.600 --> 00:10:26.770
I was too... until then.

00:10:26.770 --> 00:10:27.940
I was too... until then.

00:10:36.280 --> 00:10:38.400
That wasn't my fault!

00:10:38.400 --> 00:10:45.620
But it was such a traumatic experience that when I try to play in front of others, my hands start to shake.

00:10:46.250 --> 00:10:53.420
There is a very important traditional charity concert soon. I was supposed to play the solo, but I was forced out!

00:10:54.550 --> 00:10:56.090
Let me hear your request.

00:10:58.050 --> 00:10:58.630
Th-That's right.

00:10:58.630 --> 00:11:00.130
Th-That's right.

00:11:01.300 --> 00:11:04.810
Kerensky is to replace me.

00:11:04.810 --> 00:11:06.430
I can't allow that!

00:11:07.270 --> 00:11:09.640
Sergei Kerensky?

00:11:09.640 --> 00:11:10.770
You know him?

00:11:10.770 --> 00:11:12.440
The name.

00:11:13.060 --> 00:11:15.980
He's been my rival for years.

00:11:15.980 --> 00:11:19.990
He's popular in Russia, but I'm better than he is!

00:11:20.570 --> 00:11:25.030
However, if he succeeds here at a London Symphony Orchestra concert...

00:11:26.450 --> 00:11:29.660
I want to stop him, no matter what!

00:11:30.790 --> 00:11:34.460
I want you to hit one string on his violin during his solo.

00:11:35.710 --> 00:11:37.460
His violin string?

00:11:37.460 --> 00:11:38.840
Yeah.

00:11:38.840 --> 00:11:43.470
He's been asked to play Aria in G during his encore.

00:11:44.890 --> 00:11:49.100
Aria in G uses only the fourth string, the G String.

00:11:49.100 --> 00:11:52.480
I want you to shoot it and cause the string to break.

00:11:53.270 --> 00:11:57.520
Of course, without hurting him or the violin.

00:11:59.110 --> 00:12:04.490
I'm sure that Kerensky will panic and stand there in a daze like I did.

00:12:04.490 --> 00:12:06.700
Anybody would.

00:12:06.700 --> 00:12:12.500
If I can get the world to understand that, then my honor will be restored!

00:12:13.620 --> 00:12:17.210
Will you do it, Duke Tougou?

00:12:17.210 --> 00:12:18.500
Do you have a map of the hall?

00:12:18.500 --> 00:12:19.670
I've brought it.

00:12:22.050 --> 00:12:23.470
Slowly.

00:12:24.180 --> 00:12:24.840
O-Okay.

00:12:24.840 --> 00:12:25.720
O-Okay.

00:12:30.600 --> 00:12:32.270
This is it.

00:12:32.270 --> 00:12:36.770
Kerensky's performances are recorded on this disk.

00:12:36.770 --> 00:12:38.820
It should help.

00:12:38.820 --> 00:12:42.280
As you can see, I've prepared the requested amount.

00:12:42.820 --> 00:12:46.950
If you're Number 1, you should understand my feelings.

00:12:46.950 --> 00:12:50.290
Humiliate Kerensky!

00:13:35.830 --> 00:13:39.040
This tour is over safely, huh?

00:13:39.040 --> 00:13:41.090
It's too early to relax.

00:13:41.090 --> 00:13:44.630
The London charity concert has been added.

00:13:46.180 --> 00:13:48.430
What's going to happen?

00:13:48.430 --> 00:13:51.640
Your habits from when you were in the FBI haven't gone away yet, huh?

00:13:52.260 --> 00:13:55.730
Litvinenko was assassinated in London after he received political asylum.

00:13:56.640 --> 00:13:58.650
You haven't forgotten, have you?

00:13:58.650 --> 00:14:02.110
Kerensky is famous for his anarchist statements.

00:14:02.110 --> 00:14:04.820
We can't let our guard down.

00:14:58.580 --> 00:15:01.130
So it was you.

00:15:01.130 --> 00:15:03.710
Another crazy request, I'm sure.

00:15:04.380 --> 00:15:06.590
I want you to modify an Armalite for me.

00:15:07.590 --> 00:15:09.720
Scope magnification by 10.

00:15:10.720 --> 00:15:13.260
The lens' F-Number can be dark.

00:15:14.560 --> 00:15:19.730
And cut a screw with a 3/8th pitch into the foregrip.

00:15:21.690 --> 00:15:22.860
Is that all?

00:15:22.860 --> 00:15:23.610
Yes.

00:15:24.650 --> 00:15:30.240
I see... Anybody could do that in an hour or two.

00:15:30.240 --> 00:15:34.240
The target is a wire, 50 meters away.

00:15:35.910 --> 00:15:43.000
I get it, you're asking me 'cause you want something accurate, right?

00:15:44.500 --> 00:15:46.000
How soon can you have it done?

00:15:46.000 --> 00:15:50.130
I'll have it for you by morning.

00:16:03.150 --> 00:16:07.860
Anyway, I'm surprised you took the job of replacing Simpson.

00:16:07.860 --> 00:16:10.240
I don't consider it "replacing."

00:16:10.240 --> 00:16:12.150
I pity Simpson,

00:16:12.860 --> 00:16:16.160
but it's an honor to play with the London Symphony.

00:16:16.160 --> 00:16:18.580
That's true, but...

00:16:18.580 --> 00:16:20.660
And it's a charity concert.

00:16:20.660 --> 00:16:27.340
If it can help the children who are suffering from war and famine, I have no reason to refuse.

00:16:28.590 --> 00:16:32.550
Yes, you're right, Kerensky.

00:17:16.050 --> 00:17:18.100
I'm nobody suspicious.

00:17:18.100 --> 00:17:19.810
I want to give a bouquet to Kerensky.

00:17:20.260 --> 00:17:21.930
What?

00:17:23.060 --> 00:17:24.310
Simpson...

00:17:24.310 --> 00:17:26.850
Oh, Kerensky.

00:17:28.230 --> 00:17:29.480
He's a friend.

00:17:31.320 --> 00:17:33.900
I'll be listening from the seats today.

00:17:33.900 --> 00:17:35.610
Do your best.

00:17:36.320 --> 00:17:37.860
Thank you.

00:17:37.860 --> 00:17:40.330
I'm thankful for your friendship.

00:17:40.330 --> 00:17:42.620
I pray for your success.

00:17:42.620 --> 00:17:43.620
Goodbye.

00:17:47.250 --> 00:17:51.340
That fool Kerensky doesn't even know the hell he's about to experience.

00:18:15.860 --> 00:18:16.820
What's wrong?

00:18:18.240 --> 00:18:21.370
I saw a man carrying a metal case go past.

00:18:21.370 --> 00:18:25.790
Yes, he's going to take a video recording from the control room.

00:18:25.790 --> 00:18:29.330
He's got permission and we've confirmed his identity.

00:18:30.960 --> 00:18:33.000
So it wasn't him after all...

00:18:33.960 --> 00:18:37.380
He looked like a sniper I once knew.

00:18:37.380 --> 00:18:38.380
A sniper?

00:18:38.880 --> 00:18:41.430
A first-rate sniper.

00:18:41.430 --> 00:18:45.390
But if he was going to take out Kerensky,

00:18:46.520 --> 00:18:49.980
he wouldn't have chosen a concert hall.

00:19:04.200 --> 00:19:07.910
The London Symphony was splendid today as always.

00:19:08.660 --> 00:19:10.750
Kerensky was wonderful too.

00:19:10.750 --> 00:19:12.920
I'm looking forward to the encore.

00:20:52.520 --> 00:20:54.230
The string broke.

00:20:54.770 --> 00:20:56.270
I did it!

00:20:56.270 --> 00:20:59.270
Now Kerensky will humiliate himself too!

00:21:10.910 --> 00:21:12.580
It's a sniper!

00:21:12.580 --> 00:21:14.580
That was a bullet!

00:21:14.580 --> 00:21:15.120
What?

00:21:16.250 --> 00:21:17.130
Wait!

00:21:17.630 --> 00:21:19.290
Why are you stopping?

00:21:19.290 --> 00:21:21.130
We need to stop him.

00:21:21.130 --> 00:21:25.130
The sniper has achieved his goal.

00:21:30.140 --> 00:21:31.100
I-It can't be... he was trying to cut the string?

00:21:31.100 --> 00:21:35.690
I-It can't be... he was trying to cut the string?

00:21:35.690 --> 00:21:37.230
Probably...

00:21:37.230 --> 00:21:39.230
That's impossible!

00:21:39.230 --> 00:21:44.150
It's impossible to hit the string of a violin while it's being played!

00:21:44.950 --> 00:21:49.160
But the string was cut.

00:21:58.170 --> 00:22:05.510
That damn Kerensky... he loosened the D-string and continued to play!

00:22:10.180 --> 00:22:12.140
D-Damn!

00:22:12.140 --> 00:22:14.180
D-Damn!

00:22:42.130 --> 00:22:49.720
Chiisana koto ni zenryoku ni naru kimi no sugata yuuki ni natta hibi

00:22:42.130 --> 00:22:49.720
Those days I saw you giving your all for small things filled me with courage

00:22:49.720 --> 00:22:57.180
Zutto horyuu shippanashi jya ugokenai

00:22:49.720 --> 00:22:57.180
If I keep them suspended then I won't be able to move

00:22:59.190 --> 00:23:06.740
GARASU no HAIWEI ni tatteiru you ni

00:22:59.190 --> 00:23:06.740
It's like I'm standing on a glass highway

00:23:06.740 --> 00:23:13.950
Yume to kiken to senaka awase demo

00:23:06.740 --> 00:23:13.950
Even if I'm standing back to back with dreams and danger

00:23:13.950 --> 00:23:21.080
Kono nagai michi wo sukoshizutsu arukou

00:23:13.950 --> 00:23:21.080
I'll take this long road one step at a time

00:23:21.080 --> 00:23:27.260
Soshite kimi wa ano koro mitai ni

00:23:21.080 --> 00:23:27.260
And I need you to smile

00:23:27.260 --> 00:23:30.260
Waratteite

00:23:27.260 --> 00:23:30.260
Like you did back then

00:23:30.260 --> 00:23:36.890
Shiokaze ni yurete sasayakiatta

00:23:30.260 --> 00:23:36.890
It shook in the sea breeze and whispered

00:23:36.890 --> 00:23:47.480
Kagayaiteita tooi ano hi wa kagerou

00:23:36.890 --> 00:23:47.480
That distant and shining day is a shimmering haze

00:23:45.940 --> 00:23:49.360
The shining days

00:23:50.070 --> 00:23:55.330
Tsumaranai koto ni makeru ni wa hayasugiru

00:23:50.070 --> 00:23:55.330
I can't lose to something so trivial

00:24:01.920 --> 00:24:05.920
A mafia boss learns that Golgo is after him.

00:24:05.920 --> 00:24:12.680
To see through Golgo's quick moves, he takes a video of Golgo drawing his gun.

00:24:12.680 --> 00:24:18.100
What he saw could only be described as divine.

00:24:19.020 --> 00:24:21.350
Next time on Golgo 13:

00:24:21.350 --> 00:24:23.650
Action in 4/24.

00:24:21.390 --> 00:24:27.020
Action in 4/24

00:24:24.150 --> 00:24:28.570
Don't stand behind him if you value your life.
